## ❌ Anti-Patterns to Avoid

### Pattern 1: Loading All Secrets at Startup
```javascript
// ❌ BAD PATTERN
require('dotenv').config();
const secrets = process.env; // All secrets in memory at once
```

**Problems:**
- Secrets loaded when app starts, even if not immediately needed
- Everything loaded into process memory
- Cannot discard unused credentials
- Broad blast radius if compromised

**Better:**
```javascript
// ✅ GOOD PATTERN - Load on demand
const getRequiredSecret = (name) => {
  const secret = process.env[name];
  if (!secret) {
    throw new Error(`Secret ${name} not found`);
  }
  return secret;
};

// Get only what you need, when you need it
const maybeGetSecret = (name) => process.env[name]; // Not required
```

